    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "24. Core Abilities",
    "ruleNumber": "24.01",
    "summary": "Core abilities appear on datasheets and weapon profiles. On a weapon, the ability name is bold and bracketed. Some apply only to attacks against targets carrying at least one listed keyword. In the examples, the restriction is VEHICLE for Lethal Hits, and either INFANTRY or BEASTS for Sustained Hits 1. A check for a named ability ignores its parameter. A model with a D3 or D6 value for Deadly Demise qualifies for a check for that ability.",
